+# FAA response inventory: transcript and rerecording time labels differ
+
+October30,2026. Existing B129 /PD01–PD04 /FAA01–FAA04, supporting the REC03 original-coverage queue. **A newly acquired FAA request-and-response packet supplies specific media/transcript retrieval locators. Three paired New York end labels differ by four, two and one minutes; a Boston pair matches. These are printed-label comparisons, not verified missing audio or a reconstruction of the attacks.** The actual corrected May2003answer, delivery receipt and signed administrative disposition remain unacquired.
+
+## Acquired source and actual reading
+
+Official NARA [34913873 /AWA1077 red-tab packet](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/34913873), [direct PDF](https://catalog.archives.gov/medialive/73/9138/34913873/content/dc-metro/rg-237/7419198-9-11-faa/5-e-other/5-AWA-1077-4-Red-Tab-Commision-Request-No--2-and-AAT-20-Response-REDACT-SEALED.pdf). Acquired October30 at16:03:50–16:03:51UTC, HTTP200,application/pdf, **4,592,330bytes /26pages**, SHA256 **06bd6869f765702e620fe4344f38ab622763439979a8e9a91779ec710904ec93**. Original bytes are preserved separately from these notes. This is a released assembled scan, not native authoring/email, proof of a signed final submission, receipt, complete enclosures or complete historical holdings.
+
+Eight page images were read: **physical1,2,3,4,8,15,16,26**. Page1 is a divider. Physical8,15,16,26 print responsepages1,8,9,19. Eighteen pages were not manually read. Twenty-three pages were rendered and visible-raster OCR of8–23was used only to find headings and selected locators. Rendering/OCR is not a full26page reading. Selected readings were checked against actual images; no concealed/redacted text was reconstructed. [Reading scope](READING-SCOPE.json), [source and exact page/line pins](SOURCE-PINS.json).
+
+## What the request and response establish
+
+RequestNo2, physical2–4, asks for draft/final after-action material, interviews, FAA/NORAD and internal communications, and copies of material supplied to NTSB/FBI. Physical2 gives a **July16,2003** production date. Physical4 requests rolling production, descriptions/bases for withheld material, and locators for material outside respondent custody. These are the Commission's historical request terms, not proof every requested record was supplied or a rule adopted for any current litigation.
+
+Physical8 explicitly refers to a **July2,2003** request. The date footer on physical4 is partly occluded; this review does not reconstruct the covered characters or silently replace that observation with the response's date. Preserve the response's date attribution separately. Physical8 describes material being provided and asks another office to review answers for accuracy and suitability. That is a source-grounded review/transmittal lead; it does not authenticate the actual dispatch, acceptance, review result or completed correction.
+
+The catalog title uses **AAT-20**; the response heading on physical8 prints **AAT-200**. Both labels remain unchanged. An office-code/caption variation narrows the routing/version question; it is not evidence of falsification, and no cause or preferred code is selected.
+
+## Item16: keep every printed range
+
+Physical15/printed8 says Item16 material includes logs, a Notifications-to-Military sheet, certified transcripts and certified rerecordings. It also cross-references more material under Item20. Physical16/printed9 does the same for Item19internal communications, then begins Item20's enclosure list. Thus the following is the **Item16sub-list**, not a census of the entire production.
+
+| Conditional pairing by printed facility/role/start | Rerecording labels, as printed in UTC | Full-transcript label, as printed in UTC | Derived end-label difference |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| New York Operations Manager | **1230–1331;1331–1340** | **1230–1344** | **4minutes** |
+| New York TMU,1245start | **1245–1314** | **1245–1316** | **2minutes** |
+| New York TMU,1255start | **1255–1315** | **1255–1316** | **1minute** |
+| Boston Military Operations Specialist | **1232–1259** | **1232–1259** | **0minutes** |
+
+The original characters/ranges and selected visible-OCR lines are in [OBSERVED-LABELS.json](OBSERVED-LABELS.json), with exact physical page/line references. The arithmetic simply subtracts the latest listed rerecording end label from the transcript end label under a same-dayHHMMreading; the evidence values remain unchanged. It establishes no calibrated media duration or gap. [Code](compare_labels.py), [actual computation/source checks](VERIFICATION.json).
+
+Do **not** add these differences into a total of missing audio. The overlapping TMU entries may represent different source channels/copies; no unique channel/tape keys have been acquired. Minute precision, indexing conventions, transcript assembly, different copies/channels, additional Item20media or an actual coverage difference are untested possibilities. No explanation is selected. The matching Boston pair is retained as contrary evidence against a claim that every pair differs. These four comparisons are not four independent events or proof of intentional trimming.
+
+## How this bears on the existing correction inquiry
+
+The held AWA660note had identified Request2items3,7,16and19while retaining the broader earlier May7,2003request. The present packet supplies an actual request and a division-level response instead of only that note's description. Its **July16production date** and the earlier note's **May14due date** belong to different identified requests; they are not silently combined into one timeline. The note's reports about collection/release difficulties and the present response's affirmative provision language remain separate attributed sources. Neither alone proves complete production or nondelivery.
+
+No corrected May2003NORADanswer, delivery receipt or signed action/no-action decision is established on the pages read. The exact-title phrase occurs in the communications request itself, so a search match did not identify the original answer. Later2006disposition remains a separate target outside what a2001–2004collection can establish by search silence. Physical26 additionally names a Cleveland chain-of-custody memorandum and SATORI list; those labels are retrieval leads, not the underlying instruments or independent clock authentication. [Next records and falsifiers](OPEN-RECORDS.md).
+
+## Verification, preservation and publication limits
+
+The acquired PDF was checked for bytes/hash,26pages,zero extractable text on each page and zero enumerated embedded attachments. This does not establish absence of native attachments elsewhere. The four end-label calculations were run once against the reviewed transcription. Manual image reading is separately recorded; a parser/hash check is not independent historical authentication. No audio was acquired, listened to, decoded, aligned or repaired in this pass; no technical-owner clock test is duplicated.
+
+These notes exclude raw scan/images, full OCR/DOM, signatures, recipient/contact/personnel lists, private correspondence and case strategy. Prior sources, conflicting values and reports remain unchanged. [Checklist](CHECKLIST.md), [exact additive text diff](REVISION.diff), [manifest](MANIFEST.json). All five work-plan tracks/eighteen substantive criteria remain unfinished. Local commitment or a saved public derivative is not proof of push; publication requires separately verified account/ref/file evidence. The existing SSH publication TODO is not bypassed by a different identity or commit route.
